    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0236" n="186" xml:id="pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/52</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-04-18T19:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18, 1917,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 19, 11.45
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1200. Communicated contents of your 1324, April 16, 5 p.m., to Government which
                    greatly pleased therewith, and desires to make announcement of contents through
                    public prints. I see no objection.</p>
                <p>The plan sent to-day by military attaché to War College in his code is the result
                    of conferences between him and Russian Government.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d267-f1"
                    /> I have conferred on this subject several times with Milyukov.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d267-f2"/> We approve plan as submitted. Military attaché says
                    approved by Russian war department. I again urge prompt action for improving
                    transportation facilities. Strong practical operating man should be sent
                    Vladivostok immediately, where congestion deplorable and increasing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d267-f1" n="1" xml:id="d267-f1-content">
                <p>The plan was also received through the Russian Embassy, Apr. 21, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">infra.</hi></p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f2" n="2" xml:id="d267-f2-content">
                <p>From March to May 1917 Russian Minister of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
